/-!
# Closed embeddings into smooth varieties

Let `M` be a smooth variety over a field `k` and let `X ⟶ M` be the composite of an affine
morphism locally of finite type `f : X ⟶ Y` with a closed immersion `i : Y ⟶ M`. Then `X` is a
closed subscheme of a smooth variety over `k`: the total space of a vector bundle over `M`.

This is Fulton, *Intersection Theory*, B.8.3, by the argument of B.8.1: `M` is regular and
Noetherian with affine diagonal, so it has the resolution property; the pushforward
`(f ≫ i)_* 𝒪_X` is a quasi-coherent `𝒪_M`-algebra of finite type, generated by a quasi-coherent
`𝒪_M`-module `ℱ` of finite presentation, and `ℱ` is a quotient of a finite locally free `ℰ`; so
`X = Spec_M((f ≫ i)_* 𝒪_X)` is a closed subscheme of `𝐕(ℰ) = Spec_M(Sym ℰ)`, which is an
affine-space bundle over `M` and hence a smooth variety.

## Main results

* `MMP.exists_isClosedImmersion_vectorBundle`: over a quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme `S`
  with the resolution property, a scheme affine and locally of finite type over `S` is a closed
  subscheme, over `S`, of the vector bundle of a finite locally free `𝒪_S`-module.
* `MMP.isSmoothVariety_vectorBundleToBase_comp`: the vector bundle of a finite locally free
  module on a smooth variety is a smooth variety.
* `MMP.exists_isClosedImmersion_isSmoothVariety`: **Fulton B.8.3** for `f` affine and locally of
  finite type.
* `MMP.exists_isClosedImmersion_isSmoothVariety_of_isFinite`: the same for `f` finite.
* `MMP.isSmoothVariety_schemeProjectiveBundle_toBase_comp`: the projective bundle of a finite
  locally free module of constant positive rank on a smooth variety is a smooth variety.
* `MMP.exists_isClosedImmersion_isSmoothVariety_of_isProjective`: **Fulton B.8.3** for `f`
  projective in the sense of [Stacks, Tag 01W8], clause (1): `X` closes into `𝐏(𝒢)` over `M`
  (projective morphisms compose, Tag 0C4P), `𝒢` is a quotient of a finite locally free `ℰ` of
  positive rank, and `𝐏(𝒢) ⊆ 𝐏(ℰ)` is closed with `𝐏(ℰ)` a smooth variety.
* `MMP.exists_isClosedImmersion_isSmoothVariety_blowUp`: the same for the blowup of a closed
  subscheme of `M` in any quasi-coherent ideal sheaf (projective by Tag 02NS).

## References

* [W. Fulton, *Intersection Theory*, B.8.1 and B.8.3]
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F86](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F86)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01S8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01S8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01W8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01W8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02NS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02NS)
-/

@[expose] public section

